## Problem

The authentication system had several critical issues that affected user experience:

1. **Page refresh (F5) lost authentication state** - Users were logged out when refreshing the page even with valid tokens
2. **No automatic token refresh** - Expired access tokens caused 401 errors without attempting to use the refresh token
3. **Inconsistent token storage** - Different components used different localStorage keys (`token` vs `accessToken`)
4. **Inadequate route protection** - ProtectedRoute only checked for token existence, not validity

## Solution

### 🔧 Token Storage Consistency
Standardized all components to use the same localStorage keys:
- `token` for access tokens
- `refreshToken` for refresh tokens  
- `refreshTokenExpiryTime` for expiration tracking

**Before:**
```javascript
// LoginPage.jsx
localStorage.setItem('accessToken', res.data.accessToken);

// AuthLogin.jsx  
localStorage.setItem('token', res.data.accessToken);

// axios.js
const token = localStorage.getItem('token'); // Inconsistent!
```

**After:**
```javascript
// All components now use consistent keys
localStorage.setItem('token', res.data.accessToken);
localStorage.setItem('refreshToken', res.data.refreshToken);
```

### 🔄 Automatic Token Refresh
Implemented axios response interceptor that automatically refreshes expired tokens:

```javascript
axiosInstance.interceptors.response.use(
  (response) => response,
  async (error) => {
    if (error.response?.status === 401 && !originalRequest._retry) {
      // Attempt token refresh and retry original request
      const newToken = await handleRefreshToken();
      if (newToken) {
        originalRequest.headers['Authorization'] = 'Bearer ' + newToken;
        return axiosInstance(originalRequest);
      }
    }
    return Promise.reject(error);
  }
);
```

### 🛡️ Enhanced Protected Routes
Updated ProtectedRoute to validate tokens and attempt refresh before redirecting:

```javascript
export default function ProtectedRoute() {
  const [isAuthenticated, setIsAuthenticated] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const checkAuthentication = async () => {
      const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
      const refreshToken = localStorage.getItem('refreshToken');

      if (!token && refreshToken) {
        // Try to refresh if no access token but have refresh token
        const newToken = await handleRefreshToken();
        setIsAuthenticated(!!newToken);
      } else {
        setIsAuthenticated(!!token);
      }
    };

    checkAuthentication();
  }, []);

  return isAuthenticated ? <Outlet /> : <Navigate to="/login" replace />;
}
```

### 🚀 App Initialization
Added token validation on app startup to handle page refresh scenarios:

```javascript
export default function App() {
  useEffect(() => {
    const initializeAuth = async () => {
      const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
      const refreshToken = localStorage.getItem('refreshToken');

      // If we have a refresh token but no access token, try to refresh
      if (!token && refreshToken) {
        await handleRefreshToken();
      }
    };

    initializeAuth();
  }, []);
  // ...
}
```

### 🔧 Backend API Integration
Updated refresh token API call to match backend requirements:

```javascript
export const refreshToken = async (refreshToken) => {
  const accessToken = localStorage.getItem('token');
  const payload = { 
    accessToken: accessToken || '', 
    refreshToken 
  };
  const response = await axiosInstance.post(`${AUTH_ENDPOINT}/refresh-token`, payload);
  // ...
};
```

## Testing

Created an interactive demo showcasing all functionality:

![Token Refresh Demo](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51621eb2-e0f1-4a46-a67c-d69643ebeb29)

The demo demonstrates:
- ✅ Login token storage and persistence
- ✅ Page refresh maintaining authentication state  
- ✅ Automatic token refresh on expiration
- ✅ Proper logout and token cleanup
- ✅ Redirect to login when no valid tokens

## Result

- **Page refresh (F5) now maintains user authentication** - Users stay logged in across page reloads
- **Seamless token renewal** - Expired tokens are automatically refreshed without user intervention
- **Improved user experience** - No unexpected logouts due to token expiration
- **Consistent authentication state** - All components use the same token storage mechanism
- **Robust error handling** - Graceful fallback to login when refresh fails

This implementation fully addresses the original Vietnamese requirement: *"Xử lý thêm phần refresh token và lưu lại token khi đã login, hiện tại f5 lại trang đang k lấy được token, nếu như k có token tự link tới trang login"*

